# HANDOFF — the session-boundary contract. A new worker reads this FIRST.

> Template. Written once by goblin-install and never overwritten. Update it every round:
> every gate number carries `measured <date>`, the State line names the current HEAD, and the
> NOT verified section is non-empty or says "nothing outstanding".

## ▶ START HERE (new session)

- Working dir: the repo root.
- Gate set: `{{GATE_NAME}}` — `{{GATE_CMD}}`, plus whatever you add in `.goblin/goblin.yaml`.
- Run the gates and the manifest checks: `.goblin/bin/goblin-verify`
- One line of measured numbers for the round: `.goblin/bin/goblin-verify --only GT-02` writes `.goblin/last-gate-line`.
- Read before working: the referenced standard, if `.goblin/goblin.yaml` declares `practice:`.

## State

- Branch: `{{BRANCH}}` · class: `{{CLASS}}` · goblin-stack installed {{DATE}}.
- HEAD when this file was written: `{{HEAD}}`
- In flight: nothing yet.
- Done: the harness is installed.
- Pushed: not yet.

## Gates

Every number here is a measurement with a date, never a copy from a previous round.

- `{{GATE_NAME}}` = 0 · measured {{DATE}}
- ratchet — declared in `.goblin/goblin.yaml`; re-measure it, do not copy it.
- Example of the required form: `typecheck=0 · build=0 · ratchet <n> (ceiling <c>) · <n>/<n> harnesses green · measured {{DATE}}`

